+ IRConstantKind is U32

| constant-string = 0

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRInstruction is Struct

` A row of a function's body; its index is the id of the value it makes. `layout` is the
` layout of that value: a scalar's machine kind, or a struct, whose value is its address.
` `type` is the sealed type the value has in the source, when it has one. `aux` is the op's
` own parameter:
` - a call: the kind of its callee, whether a panic target is its last operand, and whether
`   the call records the stack of its caller for the collector;
` - arithmetic, bitwise: the operator;
` - compare: the predicate. The operands' layout says how they are compared;
` - load, address: the byte offset from the base;
` - store: the byte offset, and whether the store takes a write barrier;
` - copy, zero, frame: the layout copied, cleared or reserved, with the barrier flag;
` - load-local, store-local, local-address: the local read, written, or whose address it is;
` - load-task-word: the byte offset in the task's context of the word read;
` - float-math: the function of floats it computes;
` - return: whether it returns a panic.
` `line` and `column` count from one, and are zero for a row no source stands behind. `module`
` is the module whose file holds that source, where it is not the function's.

+ op IROp
+ block IRBlockId
+ layout LayoutId
+ type TypeId
+ syntax SyntaxId
+ line U32
+ column U32
+ operands Span
+ aux U32
+ module ModuleId = U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRBlock is Struct

` A contiguous range of instructions that ends in a terminator. A block is reserved when the
` shape that jumps to it begins, and its range starts when its turn comes.

+ instructions Span

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRLocal is Struct

` A cell of the function's frame that holds one value and is read and written whole: a local
` the source declares, or one the compiler keeps. `layout` is how its value is held.
` `address-taken` says something has the cell's address, so its value must stay in memory.
` `filled` says a call given its address fills it, as a rule's function fills where it ended.

+ layout LayoutId
+ address-taken Bool
+ filled Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRConstant is Struct

` Data a function's code addresses. A string holds its bytes with the length in characters
` and the flags its header carries.

+ kind IRConstantKind
+ bytes ByteSpan
+ character-length U32
+ flags U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRNumber is Struct

` A number the code uses, with the machine kind it is held in. A float's bits are those of
` its kind: 32 of them for the narrower one.

+ kind MachineKind
+ bits U64

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRDependency is Struct

` Something outside the function its code relies on: a function it calls, with what the call
` assumed of it.

+ kind CalleeKind
+ symbol U32
+ flags U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRStream is Struct

+ made Operand
+ begin ValueId
+ read ValueId
+ ends IdList
+ head IRBlockId = no-block
+ polled IRBlockId = no-block
+ done IRBlockId = no-block

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRNote is Struct

+ row ValueId
+ target FunctionId
+ site-module ModuleId
+ site-syntax SyntaxId
+ chain IdList

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ make-operand Operand @inline
    - kind OperandKind
    - payload U32

((kind as U32) /lshift/ operand-kind-shift) /or/ (payload /and/ operand-payload-mask)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ operand-kind OperandKind @inline
    - operand Operand

(operand /zrshift/ operand-kind-shift) as OperandKind

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ operand-payload U32 @inline
    - operand Operand

operand /and/ operand-payload-mask

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IRFunction

` One function's IR: append-only tables in the arena of the worker emitting it, reset for each
` function. `order` lists the blocks as they started, `arguments` holds the layout of each
` argument, `locals` the cells of its frame, and `returns` the layout of the value the function
` returns. `signals` says the function writes the panic signal on every return. `made-calls`
` lists the rows after which TypeScript calls a function it generates, where this IR makes in
` place what that function makes.

+ function FunctionId = no-function
+ instructions Table'IRInstruction
+ blocks Table'IRBlock
+ order IdList
+ current IRBlockId = 0
+ arguments IdList
+ locals Table'IRLocal
+ returns LayoutId
+ signals Bool
+ operands IdList
+ constants Table'IRConstant
+ numbers Table'IRNumber
+ dependencies Table'IRDependency
+ made-calls IdList
+ streams Table'IRStream
+ notes Table'IRNote
_ depended IdMap
_ arena Arena

────────────────────
+ This
    - arena Arena

.. instructions = Table'IRInstruction(arena, 16)
.. blocks = Table'IRBlock(arena, 4)
.. locals = Table'IRLocal(arena, 4)
.. constants = Table'IRConstant(arena, 4)
.. numbers = Table'IRNumber(arena, 4)
.. dependencies = Table'IRDependency(arena, 4)
.. streams = Table'IRStream(arena, 4)
.. notes = Table'IRNote(arena, 2)

────────────────────
+ do reset
    - emitted FunctionId

` Starts a function's IR over, after the arena was reset.
function = emitted
instructions = Table'IRInstruction(arena, 16)
blocks = Table'IRBlock(arena, 4)
order = IdList()
current = 0
arguments = IdList()
locals = Table'IRLocal(arena, 4)
returns = void-layout
signals = false
operands = IdList()
constants = Table'IRConstant(arena, 4)
numbers = Table'IRNumber(arena, 4)
dependencies = Table'IRDependency(arena, 4)
made-calls = IdList()
streams = Table'IRStream(arena, 4)
notes = Table'IRNote(arena, 2)
depended = IdMap()

────────────────────
+ do note-made-call

` Notes that TypeScript calls a function it generates after the last row so far.
if instructions.length != 0
    made-calls = made-calls.appended(arena, (instructions.length - 1) as U32)

────────────────────
+ do reserve-block IRBlockId

` A block to jump to, before its rows exist.
. id IRBlockId = blocks.length as IRBlockId
blocks.append(IRBlock(Span()))
= id

────────────────────
+ do start-block
    - block IRBlockId

` Begins a reserved block's rows. The blocks of a function are walked in the order they
` start.
blocks[block].instructions = Span(instructions.length as U32, 0)
order = order.appended(arena, block)
current = block

────────────────────
+ dominates Bool
    - dominator IRBlockId
    - target IRBlockId

` Whether every way the blocks started so far lead from the function's first block to a block
` passes through another, as TypeScript asks of its own blocks. A block dominates itself.
dominator == target || (reaches(target, no-block) && !reaches(target, dominator))

────────────────────
_ do reaches Bool
    - target IRBlockId
    - excluded IRBlockId

` Whether a block is reached from the function's first block by the jumps, the branches and
` the landing pads of the blocks started so far, passing through no excluded block.
if order.length == 0
    = false
. seen [Bool]
for position in 0 .. < blocks.length
    seen += false
. pending [IRBlockId]
pending += order[0]
while pending.length != 0
    . block = pending[pending.length - 1]
    pending.pop()
    if block == excluded || seen[block]
        continue
    if block == target
        = true
    seen[block] = true
    . rows = blocks[block].instructions
    for id in rows.start .. < rows.end
        if instructions[id].op != .op-phi
            . span = instructions[id].operands
            for position in span.start .. < span.end
                . operand = operands[position]
                if operand-kind(operand) == .operand-block
                    pending += operand-payload(operand)
= false

────────────────────
+ do add-argument
    - layout LayoutId

` Declares the function's next argument, in the order callers pass them.
arguments = arguments.appended(arena, layout)

────────────────────
+ do end-stream
    - stream U32
    - row ValueId

streams[stream].ends = streams[stream].ends.appended(arena, row)

────────────────────
+ do note
    - row ValueId
    - target FunctionId
    - site-module ModuleId
    - site-syntax SyntaxId
    - chain IdList = IdList()

notes.append(IRNote(row, target, site-module, site-syntax, chain))

────────────────────
+ do extended IdList
    - chain IdList
    - function FunctionId

= chain.appended(arena, function)

────────────────────
+ do add-local LocalId
    - layout LayoutId
    - address-taken Bool = false
    - filled Bool = false

` Declares a cell of the function's frame.
. id LocalId = locals.length as LocalId
locals.append(IRLocal(layout, address-taken, filled))
= id

────────────────────
+ do operand-layout LayoutId
    - operand Operand

` The layout of the value an operand stands for.
. payload = operand-payload(operand)
do match operand-kind(operand)
    |= .operand-value
        = instructions[payload].layout
    |= .operand-argument
        = arguments[payload]
    |= .operand-number
        = numbers[payload].kind
    |= .operand-constant
        = managed-layout
    |= .operand-void
        = void-layout
    ??
        = pointer-layout
= void-layout

────────────────────
+ do add-number U32
    - kind MachineKind
    - bits U64

. id U32 = numbers.length as U32
numbers.append(IRNumber(kind, bits))
= id

────────────────────
+ do add-float U32
    - kind MachineKind
    - value F64

` A float of one of the two widths, kept as its bits. The narrower one is rounded first.
if kind == .machine-f32
    . narrow = arena.allocate'F32(1)
    narrow[0] = value as F32
    = add-number(kind, (narrow as CPointer'U32)[0])
. wide = arena.allocate'F64(1)
wide[0] = value
= add-number(kind, (wide as CPointer'U64)[0])

────────────────────
+ do add-operand
    - operand Operand

operands = operands.appended(arena, operand)

────────────────────
+ do append ValueId
    - row IRInstruction

` Appends a row to the block being built, which is the one that started last.
. id ValueId = instructions.length as ValueId
instructions.append(row)
. start = blocks[current].instructions.start
blocks[current].instructions = Span(start, id + 1 - start)
= id

────────────────────
+ do add-string ConstantId
    - text String

. id ConstantId = constants.length as ConstantId
. length = text.size
. bytes = ByteSpan(arena.allocate-raw(if length != 0 then length else 1), length)
C:memcpy(bytes.data, text as CPointer'Byte, length)
. header = measure-string(bytes)
constants.append(IRConstant(.constant-string, bytes, header.character-length, header.flags))
= id

────────────────────
+ do adopt-constant
    - constant IRConstant

` Appends a constant another function's code addresses, with its bytes copied here.
. length = constant.bytes.length
. bytes = ByteSpan(arena.allocate-raw(if length != 0 then length else 1), length)
C:memcpy(bytes.data, constant.bytes.data, length)
constants.append(IRConstant(constant.kind, bytes, constant.character-length, constant.flags))

────────────────────
+ do depend
    - kind CalleeKind
    - symbol U32
    - flags U32

` Lists something the function relies on, once for each kind it is relied on as. `depended`
` holds the kinds each symbol is listed under, so a function of many callees does not read
` its list again for each call.
. listed = depended.get(symbol)
. bit = 1u32 /lshift/ (kind as U32)
if listed != no-id && (listed /and/ bit) != 0
    =
depended = depended.inserted(arena, symbol, if listed == no-id then bit else listed /or/ bit)
dependencies.append(IRDependency(kind, symbol, flags))

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ arithmetic-of U32
    - op Operator

match op
    |= .add-op
        ArithmeticOp.arithmetic-add
    |= .subtract-op
        ArithmeticOp.arithmetic-subtract
    |= .multiply-op
        ArithmeticOp.arithmetic-multiply
    |= .divide-op
        ArithmeticOp.arithmetic-divide
    |= .mod-op
        ArithmeticOp.arithmetic-remainder
    ??
        U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ bitwise-of U32
    - op Operator

match op
    |= .bitwise-and-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-and
    |= .bitwise-or-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-or
    |= .bitwise-xor-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-xor
    |= .bitwise-lshift-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-shift-left
    |= .bitwise-rshift-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-shift-right
    |= .bitwise-zrshift-op
        BitwiseOp.bitwise-shift-right-zero
    ??
        U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ predicate-of ComparePredicate
    - op Operator

match op
    |= .not-equals-op
        .compare-not-equal
    |= .less-than-op
        .compare-less
    |= .less-than-equals-op
        .compare-less-equal
    |= .greater-than-op
        .compare-greater
    |= .greater-than-equals-op
        .compare-greater-equal
    ??
        .compare-equal
